mask_static: a layer whose shapes do not change is traced once.

A contour layer's own commit marks its outline stale: it is traced again, and
the backdrop sampled and blurred again, on the next frame. That is right for
a layer whose content changes, and wasted on one that commits although
nothing did: Qt commits every mapped window of a process, with full damage,
on each frame while any animation runs in it. A desktop widget's panes are
such a window (fixed shapes under an animated text layer): 70 traces and 30
backdrop samples a second for the same picture.

hg.layer("ns", { mask_static = true }) says the shapes stay as first drawn.
The outline is still traced for the first field of a size and for
STATIC_SETTLE (1.5 s) after it, while the app may be loading what it draws,
and again whenever the size or anything else the field depends on changes.

